    "entry": "0x004b80be",
    "name": "GPIO0_607F_IRQHandler",
    "static_behavior": "Reads seven channel-0 status words into a local stack buffer, then obtains IRQ 0x3b status with enabled-only false, passes that mask to clear, then passes it to service. It ignores helper return values. The first seven-word snapshot is not subsequently read in this body."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Authenticated instruction bytes and static consumer order only; no GPIO hardware execution or callback behavior was exercised.",
    "Cached Ambiq source supports API-level semantic correspondence, not proof of the original compiler or exact build flags.",
    "The selected ISR ignores status, clear, and service return values. Callback registrations and runtime RAM table contents are external runtime state."
  ],
  "literal_words": {
    "0x00481768": {
      "meaning": "MCUN0INT0EN",
